hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4951","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ibn Zubr told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not recluse yourself in fresh water, fresh water, or fresh water, and every intoxicant is forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4952","Ishaq bin Ibrahim and Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Every drink that is intoxicating is forbidden.” The wording is from Ishaq."
"4953","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, and Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed us, on the authority of Malik Ibn Anas, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about Al-Bit’, and he said: Every drink that is intoxicating is forbidden.” The wording is by Suwayd bin Nasr."
"4954","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with him. On her authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “was asked about purchases, and he said: Every drink that intoxicates is forbidden,” and purchases of honey."
"4955","Ali bin Maimun told us, he said: Bishr bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Abd al-Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “was asked about intoxication, and he said: Every drink that causes intoxication is forbidden.” Al-Ba’ta’ is honey wine"
"4956","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Ali bin Suwayd bin Manjuf and Abdullah bin Al-Haytham bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Abu Dawud, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden.”"
"4957","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of His father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me and Muadh to Yemen, and Muadh said: You are sending us to a land of abundant drink.” Its people, so what should I drink? He said: Drink, but do not drink any intoxicating drink."
"4958","Yahya bin Musa told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Harish bin Sulaym told us, he said: Talha told us, on the authority of Abu Burdah, On the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden.”"
"4959","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Harish bin Sulaym told us, he said: Talha bin Musarrif told us, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden.”"
"4960","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, told us about the most appropriate, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi told me Musa, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to Yemen. I said: O Messenger of God, there are drinks in it, but what I drink, and what do I leave? He said: What is it? I said: Al-Bit' and Al-Mizr. He said: What are Al-Bit' and Al-Mizr?"
"4961","Muhammad ibn Adam ibn Sulayman informed us, on the authority of ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of his father, who said: “The Messenger of God sent me May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he went to Yemen, and I said: O Messenger of God, there are drinks called al-ba’t, and ale. He said: What is al-bit’? And ale? I said: A drink that is made from honey, and ale: It is made from barley. He said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4962","Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Nasr bin Ali told us, he said: my father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Nafi’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a sermon, and he mentioned the verse about wine, and a man said: Oh Messenger of God, have you seen ale? He said: What is ale? He said: A pill made in Yemen. He said: Does it intoxicate? He said: Yes. He said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. \"" 4963"""""
"4963","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu al-Juwayriyah, who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas being asked, and it was said to him: ""Give us a fatwa regarding al-Badhaq (a type of fermented drink)."" He said: ""Muhammad (ﷺ) passed away before al-Badhaq existed, but whatever intoxicates is haram."""""
"4964","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, meaning Ibn Saeed, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Amr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whatever causes intoxication in large amounts, even a small amount of it is forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4965","Humayd ibn Mukhlid informed us, he said: Sa`id ibn al-Hakam informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja`far informed us, he said: Al-Dahhak ibn Uthman informed me, On the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “He forbade you from A little of it makes a lot of it intoxicating.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4966","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, On the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He forbade a little, but a large amount of it intoxicates.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4967","Hisham bin Ammar told us, he said: Sadaqa bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Waqid, he said: Khaled bin Abdullah bin Hussein, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: I knew that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “fasting, so I encouraged him to break his fast with wine I made for him in A bear, so I brought it, and he said: Bring it closer, so I brought it closer to him, and lo and behold, it was rising, so he said: Hit the wall with it, for this is someone’s drink He does not believe in God and the Last Day.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is evidence of the prohibition of intoxicants, whether small or large, and not as much. This is what those who deceive themselves say by forbidding the last drink, and they interpret what preceded it as what had flowed through the veins before it, and there is no disagreement between the people of Knowing that drunkenness, in its entirety, does not occur with the last drink but not with the first or the second after it. By God, success."
"4968","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq On the authority of Sa`saa bin Suhan, on the authority of Ali, may God honor his face, he said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade me from using gold rings and copper. And the mitres, and the beer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4969","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid told us, on the authority of Ismail, who is Ibn Sami’, he said: Malik bin Umair told me, He said: Sa’saa bin Suhan said to Ali bin Abi Talib, may God honor his face: O Commander of the Faithful, we are against what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has forbidden. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from beasts of war, camels, and beer.”"
"4970","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was: He will be thrown into a pile of stones.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4971","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Tawus, he said: A man said to Ibn Umar: “He forbade The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Nabeez al-Jar. He said: Yes. Tawus said: By God, I heard it from him."
"4972","Harun bin Zaid bin Yazid bin Abi Al-Zarqa told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, And Ibrahim bin Maysarah said: We heard Tawus saying: A man came to Ibn Omar and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Wine of the preposition? He said: Yes. Ibrahim added in his hadith: And the bears."
"4973","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, he said: Ibn Abbas said: “He forbade The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of draft wine.”"
"4974","Ali bin Al-Hussein told us, he said: Umayyah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Jablah bin Suhaim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about the hantam. I said: What is the hantam? He said: the genitive."
"4975","4983 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Maslamah, He said: I heard Abd al-Aziz saying: Ibn al-Zubayr was asked “about the wine of the draft.” He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4976","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Ali bin Suwayd bin Manjuf informed us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about wine of ash, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it. He said hello, so I went to Ibn Abbas and said: I heard something today that surprised me. He said: What is it? I said: I asked Ibn Omar about the wine of the jar. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it. He said: Ibn Umar spoke the truth. I said: What is the preposition? He said: Everything from mudr."
"4977","Amr ibn Zurarah informed us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayya, informed us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, he said “I was with Ibn Umar.” He was asked about the wine of the jar, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it, and it was difficult for me when I heard it, so I came. Ibn Abbas, so I said: Ibn Omar was asked about something, so I began to magnify him. He said: What is it? I said: He was asked about the wine of the accusative, and he said: The Messenger of God forbade it. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: He spoke the truth. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade it. I said, “What is the preposition?” He said: “Everything is made of mud.”"
"4978","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade green wine.” I said: What about white wine? He said: I don't know"
"4979","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani told us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa saying: “It was forbidden The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of green and white draft wines. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4980","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Raja’, he said: I asked Al-Hasan, “about the wine of the genitive, Is it forbidden? He said: Forbidden. Those who did not lie told us that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the wine of camels and lizards. “And the bastards, and the naqir.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4981","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Maysara, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade scavengers.”"
"4982","4990 Ja’far bin Musafer told us, he said: Yahya bin Hassan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Ibn Tawus told us, on the authority of his father On the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade scavengers.”"
"4983","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, Hammad, and Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of stilettos and stones that are imitated.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4984","And Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, On the authority of Ali, may God honor his face, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he: “He forbade saddle-breeding and imitation things.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4985","Muhammad bin Aban Al-Balkhi told us, he said: Shababah bin Suwar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Bukayr bin Ata, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya`mar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He forbade saddlebags and imitated things.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4986","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that he told him that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He forbade wild animals, and immoral animals should be shunned.”"
"4987","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, he said: Abu Salamah told me, that he heard Aba Kitten, he says: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the animal, and it is recommended that one should be shunned from it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4988","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace: “He forbade the use of asphalt and pumpkin.”"
"4989","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abdul Khaliq Al-Shaybani. He said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab narrating, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He forbade lizards and lizards. And the horn (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4990","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, He said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade drinking from Al-Hantam, Al-Dabaa’, and Al-Naqir.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4991","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muharib, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, saying: “The Messenger forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of Al-Dabba’, Al-Hantam, and the asphalt ones."
"4992","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya told me, he said: Abu Salamah told me, he said: Abu Hurairah told me, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade jars, mounts, and fake envelopes.”"
"4993","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, saying: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Aoun bin Salih al-Bariki, on the authority of Zainab bint Nasr, and Jamila Bint Abbad, that they heard Aisha, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “It is forbidden to drink any drink made in or \Portable or artificial; it is not oil or vinegar.\"""""""
"4994","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Al-Fadl, he said: Thumamah bin Hazn Al-Qushayri told us, he said I met Aisha, and I asked her about wine. She said: The delegation of Abdul Qais came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they asked him about Do they renounce? The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade renunciation in the case of Al-Daba’, Al-Naqir, Al-Muqayyar, and Al-Hanatam. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4995","Quraysh bin Abdul Rahman informed us, he said: Ali bin Al Hassan informed us, he said: Al Hussein, who is Ibn Waqid, informed us, he said: He told me Muhammad ibn Ziyad said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He forbade the lizard, the lizard, and the hornbill.” And the asphalt (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4996","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ishaq bin Suwayd told us, on the authority of Muadhah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with him. On her behalf, she said: “He forbade beasts of war,” he began with"
"4997","And Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Ishaq, who is Ibn Suwayd, saying: Muadhah told me, On the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He forbade the wine of naqir, al-muqayir, al-dhaba’, and al-hantam,” in the hadith of Ibn Aliya: Ishaq said: Hunaida mentioned, on the authority of Aisha, a hadith similar to the hadith of Muadh, and she named the jars. I said to Hunaida: You Did you hear her name the jars? She said: Yes (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4998","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Tud bin Abdul-Malik al-Qaisi, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Hunaida bint Sharik bin Zaban said: “I met Aisha with the hadith scholar,” so I asked her about Al-Akr, but she forbade me from it, and said: “Give it away in the evening, and drink it in the morning, and you have commanded me to do what I am instructed to do, and you have forbidden me from the dabba’, the naqir, the tamzafat, and the hantamah.”"
"4999","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, he said: I heard Al-Mukhtar bin Fulfil, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace from the false circumstances.”"
"5000","5008 Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Mansour bin Hayyan told us, he heard Ibn Jubayr, speaking He heard Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas testify against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he forbade lizards and lizards. And Al-Muzaffat, and Al-Naqir. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this verse: And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you from it. So they finished\"" 5001"""""
"5001","Suwayd ibn Nasr informed us, saying: 'Abdullah informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Asma' bint Yazid, from a paternal cousin of hers named Anas, who said: Ibn 'Abbas said: ""Did not Allah, Mighty and Majestic, say: 'And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it' (59:7)?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Did not Allah say: 'And it is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decided a matter, that they should have any choice in their affair' (33:36)?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Then I bear witness that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) forbade the Naqir, the Muqayyar, the Dubba', and the Hantam (names of vessels used for fermenting drinks)."""""
"5002","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Amr bin Murrah told me, he said: I heard Zazan, he said: I asked Abdullah bin Omar, I said: Tell me something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “in the vessels” and explain it. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the hantam, which is what you call the jarr, and he forbade the scavenger, which is the one. You call it gourd, and he forbade the niqir, which is the palm tree, which they peck, and he forbade the pure, which is the palm tree."
"5003","Siwar bin Abdullah bin Siwar told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the delegation of Abd al-Qais when they came to him from lizards, from al-Naqir, and from al-mzafat. And Al-Mazad Al-Majoubah, and he said: “Come away from your watering can, give it a taste, and drink it sweet.” Some of them said: Permit me, O Messenger of God, to “Like this,” he said: “Then you make it like this,” and he gestured with his hand to describe it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5004","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, a reading, he said: And Abu Al-Zubayr said, I heard Jabir, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the jird, the tambourine, the lizard, and the horn. If the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not find A water-drink is thrown out for him, and a pile of stones is thrown out for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5005","Ahmad bin Khalid told me, he said: Ishaq told us, meaning Al-Azraq, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, On the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to: “We will abandon him in a water-tender, and if he does not have a water-tender, we will abandon him in a water-trail.” Baram, he said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the tambourine, the niqir, and the imitated one."
"5006","Siwar bin Abdullah bin Siwar told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Abdul Malik told us, he said: Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He forbade the tambourine, the horn, the jird, and the tamper.”"
"5007","Ibrahim bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Sulayman al-Ahwal told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Iyad, on the authority of Abd By God, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “made a concession in the preposition that is not simultaneous.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5008","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas bin Jawab, on the authority of Ammar bin Ruzaiq, that he told them, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I forbade you from eating meat. Sacrifices after three days, and abstain from wine except when drinking water, and from visiting graves, so eat from the meat of the sacrificial animals as much as you like, and provide for yourself and save up. And whoever wants to visit the graves, it reminds him of the Hereafter, and drink, and beware of every intoxicant.”"
"5009","Muhammad bin Adam bin Sulayman told me, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, On the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have forbidden you from visiting graves, so visit them, and I have forbidden you from the meat of sacrificial animals above “For three days, abstain from whatever you like, and I forbade you from wine except from water-troughs, so drink from all water-troughs, and do not drink any intoxicating drink.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5010","Muhammad bin Ma’dan bin Issa bin Ma’dan informed us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ayan told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Zubaid told us, On the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I had forbidden you from three things: Visiting graves, so visit them and may their visit increase your goodness. I forbade you from sacrificial meat after three days, so eat from it whatever you wish. I forbade you Concerning drinks in vessels, so drink from any vessel you wish and do not drink any strong drink.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5011","Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Al-Hajjaj told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Abi Suleiman, On the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I forbade you from vessels, so shun them.” Whatever appears to you, and beware of every intoxicant.”"
"5012","Abu Ali Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Marwazi told us, he said: Abdullah bin Uthman told us, he said: Issa bin Ubaid Al-Kindi told us, He said: I heard Abdullah bin Buraydah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “While he was traveling, he came upon a people and heard They had a murmur, so he said: What is this sound? They said: O Prophet of God, they have something to drink. So he sent to the people and called for them, and he said: What do you choose to do? They said: We choose to do so in al-Naqir and al-Dabaa’, and we have no conditions. He said: Do not drink except what you have been trained to do. He remained in that state for as long as God wished for him to remain, then returned to them, and behold, an epidemic had struck them and they had turned yellow. He said: What is the matter with me when I see you? Have you perished? They said: O Prophet of God, our land and environment have been forbidden to us except what we have been given permission to do. He said: Drink, and every intoxicant is forbidden. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5013","5021 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan informed us, saying: Abu Dawud al-Hafari and Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “When he forbade the circumstances, the Ansar complained and said: O Messenger of God, we do not have A container, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to the Ansar, and she said: O Messenger of God, we do not have a container, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Then no. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5014","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, informed us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “Two cups of wine and milk were brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night he was taken captive, and he looked at them. So he took the milk, and Gabriel, peace be upon him, said to him: Praise be to God who has guided you to the right path. If you took wine, your nation would go astray."
"5015","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Khaled, who is Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Shu’bah, who said: I heard Abu Bakr bin Hafs, saying: I heard Ibn Muhayriz, speaking on the authority of a man from the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “People drink from... My nation of wine, they call it by another name.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5016","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Uqail, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The adulterer does not commit adultery when he commits adultery while he is a believer, and the one who drinks it does not drink alcohol.” When he drinks it while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal when he is a believer, and he does not plunder such a thing that people raise their eyes to him when He seizes it while he is a believer.”"
"5017","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab told me And Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, all of them narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The adulterer does not commit adultery when He commits adultery while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal when he steals while he is a believer, and he does not drink alcohol when he drinks it while he is a believer, and he does not plunder An honorable plunder to which Muslims raise their eyes, and he is a believer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5018","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Na’am, on the authority of Ibn Umar and a group of people. Among the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, they said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever drinks alcohol, flog him, then if he drinks Then flog him, then if he drinks, flog him, then if he drinks, kill him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5019","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Shababah told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of his uncle Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman. On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “If he gets drunk, flog him, then if he gets drunk, flog him. Then if he gets drunk, flog him. Then he said on the fourth day: “Behead him.”"
"5020","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala informed us, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Wa’il Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abu Burdah bin Abi Musa, on the authority of his father, Radi God said on his authority, that he used to say: “I don’t care if I drink wine or worship this idol instead of God Almighty.”"
"5021","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Othman bin Hisn told us, he said: Urwa bin Ruwaym told us, that Ibn al-Dailami rode, So he asked for Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas. Ibn Al-Dailami said: So I entered upon him and said: Have you heard, O Abdullah bin Amr, Messenger of God? Did he, may God bless him and grant him peace, mention anything about alcohol? He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A man from my nation does not drink alcohol, and God will accept forty prayers from him.” \one day\"""""""
"5022","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith, on the authority of his father, said: I heard Othman, may God be pleased with him, saying: “Avoid alcohol, for it is the mother of all evil. He was a man Whoever went before you to worship, then a seduced woman made him stop, so she sent her maid to him, and she said to him: I am calling you to witness, so he set off. With her maid, so whenever he entered a door she closed it for him, until he led to a modest woman, who had a boy and a veil of wine. She said: By God, I did not call you to witness, but I called you to come against me, or to drink a cup of this wine, or to be killed. This boy, he said: Give me a cup of this wine to drink, so I gave him a cup to drink, and he said: Give me more, so he did not throw until he fell on it and killed the person. So avoid alcohol, for by God, faith and addiction to alcohol do not go together unless one of them is about to expel its companion.” Suwaid told us. Ibn Nasr, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Bakr Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn al-Harith narrated to me, that His father, he said: I heard Uthman saying: “Avoid alcohol, for it is the mother of all evils, for a man who passed away before you used to worship, And the people will isolate themselves.” Then he mentioned a similar example, saying: “Avoid alcohol, for by God it is never combined with faith unless it is about to go out.” \One of them is his friend.\"""""""
"5023","Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Surayj bin Yunus told us, he said: Yahya bin Abdul Malik told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, who is the son of Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “Whoever drinks alcohol and does not get high, his prayer will not be accepted as long as it is inside him.” Or some of it is in his veins, and if he dies, he dies as a disbeliever, and if he gets drunk, his prayers will not be accepted for forty nights, and if he dies therein, he dies as a disbeliever. Yazid bin Abi Ziyad"
"5024","Muhammad ibn Adam ibn Sulayman informed me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahim, on the authority of Yazid, and Wasil ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, saying: Ibn al-A’la informed us. Fudayl, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Who He drank wine and placed it in his stomach, and seven prayers would not be accepted from him. If he died during them, he would die as an unbeliever. If his mind was taken away from any of obligatory duties, his prayers will not be accepted for forty days, and if he dies, he dies as an unbeliever.” And the wording is “wasil.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5025","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, He said: Rabia bin Yazid told me. H And Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed told me, on the authority of Baqiya, on the authority of Abi Amr, who is Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Rabi’a bin Yazid, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn al-Dailami said: I entered upon Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-Aas, and he was in his neighborhood in Taif. He was called al-Waht, and he was A young man from Quraysh committed adultery by drinking alcohol. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever drinks alcohol If he drinks, his repentance will not be accepted for forty mornings. If he repents, God will repent to him. If he returns, his repentance will not be accepted for forty mornings. If He repents, God will accept his repentance, and if he returns, it is God’s duty to give him to drink from the clay of spoils on the Day of Resurrection.” The wording by Amr"
"5026","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading it and pronouncing it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever drinks alcohol in this world and then does not He will repent from it and be deprived of it in the Hereafter.”"
"5027","Muhammad ibn Bashhar informed us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Nabit, on the authority of Jaban, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “No immoral person, no disobedient person, and no alcoholic will enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5028","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever drinks alcohol in this world and dies while addicted to it will not repent of it. He will not drink it in the afterlife.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5029","Yahya bin Durst told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever drinks alcohol in this world and dies while addicted to it will not drink it in the Hereafter.”"
"5030","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Abd al-Ala bin Hammad told us, he said: Mu’tamar bin Sulayman told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told me. On the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Al-Musayyab, he said: “Umar, may God be pleased with him, took Rabi’ah ibn Umayyah to Khaybar in wine, So he joined Heraclius and became a Christian, and Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: I will not go abroad as a Muslim after him.”"
"5031","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Simmak, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Burdah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Drink under circumstances, and do not become drunk.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith, and it was erroneous in it. Abu Al-Ahwas Salam bin Sulaym. We do not know that any of the companions of Samak bin Harb followed him against him, and Samak was not strong and he used to accept Indoctrination, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ahmad ibn Hanbal said: Abu al-Ahwas made mistakes in this hadith, and a partner disagreed with him in its chain of transmission. And in his wording"
"5032","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He forbade the lizard, the hantam, the niqir, and the saddlebag, and then he said: Indeed, I have forbidden you from any circumstances, so abstain from whatever you like and avoid every intoxicant.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Awanah disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5033","Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Hajjaj told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Qarafat. A woman among them, on the authority of Aisha, said: “Drink and do not get drunk.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This also is not proven, and it is a qirsafa. We do not know who this woman is. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: What is known about Aisha is the opposite of what Qarsafa narrated about her."
"5034","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Qadamah Al-Amiri, that Jasra bint Dajjah Al-Amiriyya told him, She said: I heard Aisha. People asked her, all of them asking about wine. They say: We reject the dates in the morning and drink them in the evening. And we make it in the evening and drink it in the morning? She said: I do not permit an intoxicant, even if it is bread, or if it is water. She said it three times."
"5035","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Mubarak, he said: Karima bint Hammam told us, that I heard Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, say: “You are forbidden from sexual intercourse, you are forbidden from having sexual intercourse, you are forbidden from immoral things.” Then she turned to women. She said: “Beware of green water. If the water of your love makes you intoxicated, do not drink it.”"
"5036","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Aban bin Samaa told us, he said: My mother told me, on the authority of Aisha She was asked about drinks, and she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade every intoxicant.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: They relied on the hadith of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas."
"5037","Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Al-Qawariri told us, he said: Abd al-Warith told us, he said: I heard Ibn Shubrumah mentioning him. On the authority of Abdullah Ibn Shaddad Ibn Al-Had, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Alcohol was forbidden, whether it is little or much, and intoxication from any drink is forbidden.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Ibn Shubruma did not hear it from Abdullah bin Shaddad."
"5038","Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Suraij bin Yunus told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Shubrumah, he said: Al-Thiqah told me, On the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Wine itself was forbidden, both small and large, and intoxicants of every kind of drink.” He disagreed with him. Abu Aoun Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Thaqafi (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5039","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad told us, and Al-Hussein bin Mansour informed us, he said: Ahmad bin Hanbal, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “Wine itself was forbidden, both small and large, and intoxication from every drink.” Ibn al-Hakam did not mention: a small amount of it. And many of them (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5040","Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Abbas told us, he said: A partner told us, On the authority of Abbas bin Dhurayh, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Alcohol was forbidden, whether it is little or much. “And nothing is more intoxicating than any drink.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is more correct than the hadith of Ibn Shubrumah, and Hushaym bin Bashir was He deceives, and there is no mention in his hadith of hearing from Ibn Shubrumah, and the narration of Abu Aoun is more similar to what the trustworthy narrators narrated on the authority of Ibn Abbas.”"
"5041","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Juwayriyah Al-Jarmi, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas, while he was leaning his back. To the Kaaba, “on the authority of Al-Badhiq, and he said: Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, preceded Al-Badhiq, and whatever intoxicates is forbidden.” He said: I am the first of the Arabs. He asked him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5042","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abu Amir informed us, an-Nadr ibn Shumail, and Wahb ibn Jarir informed us, they said: Shu`bah told us. On the authority of Salamah bin Kuhail, he said: I heard Abu Al-Hakam speaking, Ibn Abbas said: “Whoever is pleased to enter into a state of ihram, if he is in a state of ihram, what God has made prohibited.” And His Messenger, let him make wine forbidden.”"
"5043","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, he said: A man told Ibn Abbas “I am a person from the people of Khorasan, and our land is a cold land. We drink raisins, grapes, and other things, and it has become difficult for me.” So he mentioned various kinds of drinks to him, and he added so much to the point that I thought he did not understand it, so Ibn Abbas said to him: You have done too much for me. “Avoid anything that is intoxicating, such as dates, raisins, or anything else.”"
"5044","Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Al-Qawariri told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Pure pure wine is not permissible.”"
"5045","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Jamrah, he said: I was translating between Ibn Abbas. And among the people, a woman came to him asking him about pure wine, but he forbade it. I said: O Ibn Abbas, “I sip it in a green jar.” “Sweet wine, so I drink some of it and it makes my stomach growl.” He said: “Do not drink from it, even if it is sweeter than honey.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5046","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Attab told us, he is Sahl bin Hammad, he said: Qurrah told us, he said: Abu Jamarat Nasr told us He said: I said to Ibn Abbas: My grandmother throws wine in a jar. I drink it sweet. If I drink a lot of it, then I sit with the people, fearing that I will be exposed. He said: “The delegation of Abdul Qais came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: The delegation is welcomed, neither disgraced nor remorseful. They said: O Messenger of God! Indeed, between us and you are polytheists, and we do not reach you except during the sacred months, so inform us of a matter that if we act upon it, we will enter. Paradise, and we invoke it from behind us. He said: I command you to do three, and I forbid you to do four: I command you to believe in God, and do you know what faith is? By God? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: Bearing witness that there is no god but God, and establishing prayer, and paying zakat, and that you give from “The five spoils of spoils, and I forbid you from four: that which is forbidden in al-Daba’ab, al-Naqir, al-Hantam, and the mixed ones.”"
"5047","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Qais bin Hanan, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas, I said: “I have a drink from which I shun it. When it boils and settles, I drink it.” He said: “How long has this been your drink?” I said: Twenty years ago, or he said: Forty years ago, he said: As long as your veins are cleansed of impurity. Nafi’ on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar"
"5048","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: The common people told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Nafi’, he said: Ibn Umar said “I saw a man who came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a cup of wine in it, and he was at a corner. The cup was given to him, and he raised it to He found it severe, so he returned it to its owner, and a man from among the people said to him: O Messenger of God, is it forbidden? He said: The man was brought to me, so he was brought With it, he took the cup from it, then called for water and poured it into it, then he raised it to his bowl and frowned, then he called for water also and poured it into it, then He said: “If these containers become hard for you, break their rims with water,” and Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, he said: Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a similar manner. He said Abu Abd al-Rahman: Abd al-Malik ibn Nafi’ is not well-known and his hadith cannot be taken as evidence, and what is known on the authority of Ibn Umar is the opposite of his story. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5049","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that a man He asked him “about drinks,” and he said: “Avoid everything that intoxicates.”"
"5050","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about drinks. He said: “Avoid everything that excites you.”"
"5051","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “ Intoxicants, whether small or large, are forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5052","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard a young man, who is Ibn Abdul-Malik, saying: A fighter told me Ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Salem Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God forbade wine, and every intoxicant \Forbidden\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"5053","Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr informed us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden, and every intoxicant is alcohol.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: These are the people of Steadiness and justice are famous for the accuracy of transmission, and Abd al-Malik does not take the place of any one of them, even if a group supports him in any form. And God grant us success (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5054","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar Al-Sa’idi, he said: Ruqayyah bint Amr bin Saeed, she said: “I was in Ibn Omar’s lap, and he used to soak raisins for him, and he would drink them the next day, then the raisins would be dried, and raisins would be thrown on them.” Another, and water is put in it, and he drinks it from the next day, until when the day after the next comes, he throws it away.” They used as evidence the hadith of Abu Masoud Uqba bin Amr"
"5055","Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Suleiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Yaman informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Khalid bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Masoud, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was thirsty near the Kaaba, so he drew water, and wine was brought from the water-taker. He smelled it, frowned, and said: I am guilty of some sins from Zamzam. So he poured it on him and then drank, and a man said: Is it forbidden, O Messenger of God? He said: No. He said Abu Abdul Rahman: This is weak news. Because Yahya bin Yaman was the only one to do it without the companions of Sufyan, and Yahya bin Yaman does not take his hadith as evidence due to his poor memorization and many mistakes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5056","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Othman bin Hisn told us, he said: Zayd bin Waqid told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Hussein, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah said: I knew that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast on some of the days he used to fast, so I checked to break his fast. With wine I made it into a bowl, and when evening came I came to carry it to him, and I said: O Messenger of God, I know that you are fasting on this occasion! Today, I refreshed your breakfast with this wine, and he said: Bring it closer to me, Abu Hurairah. So I pushed it to him, and it was ripening. He said: Take it. This, then hit the wall with it, for this is the drink of one who does not believe in God or in the Last Day.” Among what they used as evidence was the action of Omar ibn Al-Khattab May God be pleased with him"
"5057","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Al-Sari bin Yahya, he said: Abu Hafs, our imam, and he was one of the Asan Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: “If you are afraid of a wine that is too strong, break it with water.” Abdullah said: That is, before it becomes severe."
"5058","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, Saeed bin Al-Musayyab heard He says: “Thaqif asked Omar ibn al-Khattab for a drink, so he called for it, but when he brought it to his mouth he hated it, so he called for it and broke it with water, and said: “This is what you do.”"
"5059","Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Khaythamah told us, he said: Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Ubayy told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jahadah, On the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qays bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Utbah bin Farqad, he said: “The wine that Omar bin Al-Khattab drank was “And what indicates the authenticity of this is the hadith of Al-Sa’ib (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5060","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz told us, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that a man from Two armies, and two armies from Yemen, came and asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “about a drink they drink in their land of corn, which is called Bitter, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And is it an intoxicant? He said: Yes. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. God Almighty has made a covenant with whoever drinks intoxicants to give him drink of the clay of vinegar. They said: O Messenger of God, and what is the clay of vinegar? The people of Hell, or he said: the juice of the people of Hell. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5061","Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “What is permissible is clear, and what is forbidden is clear, and between these are doubtful matters.” And he may have said: And in between that there are doubtful matters, and I will give an example of that: God Almighty has protected, and God has protected what He has forbidden, and He is the one who takes care of Concerning fever, he is about to be afflicted with fever, and he may have said: he is about to be shaken, and he who is mingled with doubt is about to become afflicted.”"
"5062","Muhammad ibn Aban informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris informed us, he said: Shu`bah informed us, on the authority of Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abu Al-Hawraa Al-Saadi said: I said to Al-Hasan bin Ali, may God be pleased with them both: What did you memorize from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I learned from him: “Leave what doubts you for what does not doubt you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5063","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Dinar, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, he said: “Saad had vineyards.” And many grapes, and he had a trustee in them, so I carried many grapes, so he wrote to him: I fear for the lost grapes, so if you see that I squeezed him, and I squeezed him, so Saad wrote to him: When this letter of mine comes, withdraw from my estate, for by God I will never trust you with anything after that. So he isolated him from his village.”"
"5064","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Nubaata, on the authority of Suwayd bin Inadvertently, he said: “Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to some of his workers: Provide the Muslims with paint, two-thirds of which is gone and a third of which remains.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5065","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Dawud, he said: I asked Saeed, “What is the drink that Omar, may God be pleased with him, made permissible?” About him? He said: “The one that is cooked until two-thirds of it is gone and one-third remains.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5066","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Aamir bin Abdullah, he said: I read the letter of Omar ibn al-Khattab to Abu Musa: “As for what follows, a camel came to me from the Levant carrying a thick drink black like camel paint. And I asked them how much they cook it for, and they told me that they cook it for two-thirds, two-thirds of which are gold, one-third of which is khabthan. With its iniquity and a third with its odor, so pass by those before you who may drink it.”"
"5067","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Khattimi, said Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, wrote to us: “As for that, cook your drink until Satan’s portion goes away from it, for he has two And there is one for you.”"
"5068","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ash-Shabi, he said: “Ali used to provide people with paint that fell There are flies in it, and they cannot get out of it.”"
"5069","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Hushaym, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid informed us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, that: “He used to drink from the paint, of which two-thirds had gone and one-third remained.”"
"5070","5085 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Hammad told us, and Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said : Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyib, that Abu Al-Darda’ “used to drink what two-thirds of it was gone and one-third of it remained.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"5071","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Saad bin Aws told us, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik said: “Noah, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was disputed by Satan regarding a vineyard, and this man said: This is for me, and this man said: This is for me. So they agreed that one-third of it would belong to Noah, and two-thirds of it would belong to Satan."
"5072","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Abu Ya`four al-Salami, on the authority of Abu Thabit al-Thaalabi, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas, then a man came to him and asked him about the juice. He said: Drink it while it is fresh. He said: I made a drink while some of it was on my soul. He said: Did you Did you drink it before you cooked it? He said: No. He said: Fire does not make lawful anything that has been forbidden."
"5073","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, a reading, he said: Ata’ told me, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, He says: “By God, fire does not dissolve anything but does not make it unlawful.” He said: Then he explained to me his saying: It does not dissolve anything: according to what they say about paint, and it does not make it unlawful: ablution from among \fire touched\"""""""
"5074","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir told me, he said: Baqiyya told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Amr, On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Dailami, on the authority of his father Fayrouz, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God! “We are the owners of a vineyard, and God Almighty has revealed the prohibition of wine, so what should we do? He said: Do you take it as raisins? I said: So we will make it.” With raisins, what? He said: You soak it for your lunch and drink it for your dinner, and you soak it for your dinner and drink it for your lunch, I said: Should we not delay it until it becomes severe? He said: Do not put it in hardship, but put it in hardship, for if it is delayed, it will become empty."
"5075","Issa bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Damra, on the authority of Al-Sibani, on the authority of Ibn Al-Dailami, on the authority of his father, he said: We said: O Messenger of God, “Indeed, we Grapes, what do we do with them? He said: Raisins. We said: What do we do with raisins? He said: Sprinkle them in your food and drink them with your dinner? Sprinkle it with your dinner and drink it with your food, and sprinkle it in the evening, and do not sprinkle it in the frying pan, for if it is delayed it becomes vinegar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5076","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Muti’ told us, on the authority of Abu Omar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “He was rejected. to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he drinks it the next day and the day after. When it is the evening of the third day, if there is anything left in the vessel, They drink it. He ordered it and it was poured out.”"
"5077","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Ubaid. Al-Bahrani, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to soak raisins for him, and he would drink them every day and the next. \And the day after tomorrow\"""""""
"5078","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya Abi Umar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God was May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Raisin wine is made for him at night, and he puts it in a waterskin, and he drinks it that day, and the next day, and the day after.” Tomorrow, if it was from the last of the third day, he gave it to drink or drank it, and if he had any of it in the morning, he spilled it.”"
"5079","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that it was: “He will be rejected in He would pour waterskins of raisins in the morning, and he would drink them during the night, and he would throw them away in the evening and drink them in the morning. He would wash the waterskins, and would not make There is nothing in it. Nafi’ said: We used to drink it like honey."
"5080","Suwayd informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Suleiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, and not by al-Nahdi, that Umm al-Fadl sent to Anas bin Malik asked him “about the wine of the genitive.” He told her on the authority of his son Al-Nadr, that: “He throws out wine in the genitive, he throws it out in the morning. And he drinks it in the evening.”"
"5081","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Asad bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, He said: Umm Sulaim had a cup, and she said: “I made the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drink everything in it: water, honey, milk, and wine.”"
"5082","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Dhar bin Abdullah, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, he said: “I asked Ubayy Ibn Ka’b” about wine, and he said: Drink water, and drink honey, And drink the fruit, and drink the milk with which I was nourished. So I went back to him, and he said: Do you want wine? Do you want wine? \"" 5083"""""
"5083","Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Sa'id ibn Ibrahim informed me, saying: Al-Qawariri narrated to us, saying: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad, from 'Ubaydah, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: ""People have invented drinks the nature of which I do not know; I have had no drink for twenty years, or he said forty years, except water and sawiq (barley broth),"" except that he did not mention nabidh (fermented date drink)."
"5084","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, he said: “The people narrated “I don’t know what they are, and I have had no drink for twenty years except water, milk, and honey.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5085","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Ibn Shubrumah, he said: Talha said to the people of Kufa, “Concerning wine: temptation.” The young grow up therein, and the old grow old therein. He said: Whenever there was a wedding party among them, Talhah and Zubair would water the milk and honey. It was said to Talha: Will you not give them wine to drink? He said: I hate for a Muslim to get drunk because of me."
"5086","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: I am Yazid, and he is Ibn Zuray’. He said: Sa’id bin Abi Arouba told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Danaj told us, he said: I heard Hudayn ibn al-Mundhir that al-Walid ibn Utba “led the people of Kufa to the morning prayer with four rak’ahs, then he said: Shall I add more to you?” He said: So he testified against him before Uthman that he had drunk alcohol, so Ali said to Uthman: Perform the punishment on him. He said: Below you is your cousin, so perform the punishment on him. He said: Get up, O Hussein, and flog him. What are you doing with this and anyone else? He said: Rather, I am weak, weak, and helpless. Get up, O Abdullah bin Jafar. So flog him, he said: So he started flogging him, and Ali counted until he reached forty, so he said: Hold it, he flogged the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu A virgin for forty, and he completed it at the age of eighty, and every year.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5087","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us. He said: I am Yahya bin Hammad. He said: Abdul Aziz bin Al-Mukhtar told us. He said: Abdullah bin Fayrouz told us. Mawla bin Amir Al-Danaj, he said: Husayn bin Al-Mundhir Abu Sasan told us, he said: Ali said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was flogged forty. Abu Bakr forty, and Umar eighty, and each year.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5088","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed al-Nakhi, he said: Ali said: “There is no man over whom I have performed a punishment and he dies, and I find myself in it, except wine. If he dies, I will pay his blood money for it. Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He did not enact it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5089","Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Ahmad bin Abi Shuaib told us, he said: Musa told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, he said: I heard Ali, saying: “Whoever we impose a punishment on him and he dies from it, no blood money is owed to him, except for the one whom we beat with wine, for it is just something.” \We made it\"""""""
"5090","Al-Hasan bin Al-Sabbah Al-Bazzar told us, he said: Shababah bin Suwar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “A man was brought who had drunk alcohol, and he hit him with two newspapers for about forty.”"
"5091","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Qatada told us, he said: I heard Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God was brought May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he met a man who had drunk alcohol, so he hit him with two newspapers for about forty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5092","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought “And he greeted a man who had drunk alcohol, and flogged him with two strips of about forty,” and Abu Bakr did that. When Omar was gone, he consulted the people. He said: The lightest punishment is eighty, so Omar ordered that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5093","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought A man who had drunk alcohol, and he struck him with his sandals about forty times, then Abu Bakr was brought to him, and he did the same thing, then Omar was brought to him. So he mentioned something similar"
"5094","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that he mentioned that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him: “He was flogged in wine with a cloth and sandals.”"
"5095","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Asad bin Musa told us, he said: Hatim bin Ismail told us, he said: Al-Ja’id bin Abd told us. The Most Gracious, he said: I heard Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid saying: “We were in the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, and some of the time of Omar until they rebelled. Therein, meaning: in wine, so he flogged them forty, but they did not eat, so he flogged eighty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5096","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Abu Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Al-Ja’id bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid said: “We used to bring the drinker during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the era of Abu Bakr, and he came from an emirate Omar, so we stand up to him and beat him with our hands, our cloaks, and our sandals, until he was in the midst of Omar’s emirate, and he was flogged there for forty, until he rebelled. And they committed immoral acts, he was flogged therein by eighty people.”"
"5097","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Mekki told us, he said: Al-Mu’alla bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusayfa, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid said: “We used to bring the drinker during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and during the command of Abu Bakr, and some of Omar’s wife, so we will rise up and strike him with our hands, our sandals, and our cloaks.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5098","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Usama, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Azhar said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hunayn asking about Khalid’s house, and a drunk man was brought.” So the Messenger of God ordered May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, whoever was with him should hit him with whatever they had in their hands, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, urged him to throw dust on him, so when he Abu Bakr was brought drunk, so he took aim at the one who had beaten them that day, so he struck forty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5099","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Abd al-Rahman bin Azhar told us, He was speaking: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was present when he was throwing dust on their faces.”"
"5100","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, saying: In the book of Khali, on the authority of Uqayl, that Ibn Shihab informed him, that Abdullah ibn Abd Al-Rahman Al-Zuhri told him, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “A drinker was brought on the day of Hunayn and they threw dust in his face. Then he ordered his companions to hit him with their sandals and whatever was in their hands, until he said to them: Take it down. They did so, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. “peace be upon him, and that is a Sunnah.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is more correct than the one before it."
"5101","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Sadran told me, he said: Azhar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Azhar reported that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “A drunk man was brought and he said: Hit him.” So they hit him with their sandals. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5102","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Azhar said: “A drinker was brought, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Get up to him and beat him, so the people got up.” So they hit him with their sandals.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5103","Abdullah bin Al-Sabbah bin Abdullah told us, he told us: Mu`tamir told us, he said: I heard Muhammad speaking, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Azhar, said: “A drinker was brought to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the day of Hunayn, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Get up and hit him.” Then the people got up and hit him with their sandals. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5104","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Anas bin Iyadh told me, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salama Ibn Abdul Rahman, Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “A man was brought who had drunk, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: “Strike him.” Among us is the one who strikes with his hand, the one who strikes with his shoe, and the one who strikes with his clothing. When he left, he said: This means: The people whom God has disgraced. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not say like that, do not help Satan in this, but say: May God have mercy on you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5105","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi told us, he said: Saeed bin Ufayr told us, he said: Yahya bin Falih bin Suleiman Al-Madani told us, On the authority of Thawr ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “In the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drinkers were beaten with their hands.” And sandals and sticks, until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, and they were more in the caliphate of Abu Bakr than they were in the era of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then Abu Bakr said: If we imposed a punishment for them, then we were to aim for what they used to strike during the era of the Messenger of God, so it was. Abu Bakr flogged them for forty until he died, then Omar was after him, so he flogged them forty as well, until a man from the first immigrants was brought. He had drunk, so he ordered him to be flogged, and he said: Why do you flog me? There is a book of God between you and me. Omar said: What book of God do you find that you do not? Did he flog you? He said to him: Indeed, God says in His Book: There is no blame on those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted the verse, for I am of those who believe. And they did righteous deeds, then they feared and believed, then they feared and did good. I witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Badr and Uhud. And the trench, and the scenes. Omar said: Will you not respond to what he says? Ibn Abbas said: These verses were revealed as an excuse for the past, and as a proof. For those who remain, the excuse for those who passed by is that they met God before alcohol was forbidden to them, and an argument for those who remain, because God says: O Those who believe, wine, gambling, stones, and arrows are only an abomination, the work of Satan. The verse. Then he also read the other verse: Then if he is of those They believed and did righteous deeds, then they feared and believed, then they feared and did good, for God had forbidden him from drinking alcohol, so Omar said: You are right. So what do you think? He said: Is it that when he drinks he gets drunk, and when he gets drunk he slanders, and when he slanders he slanders, and the slanderer is liable to eighty lashes, so he ordered. Omar was flogged for eighty years (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5106","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, he said: Yahya bin Falih bin Suleiman told us, he said: Thawr ibn Zayd al-Dili told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “Qudama ibn Mazun drank alcohol in Bahrain, and he testified On it, then he was asked and he admitted that he drank it, so Omar bin Al-Khattab said to him: What made you do that? He said: Because God says: It is not for those who They believed and did righteous deeds. They will be rewarded with what they ate, so long as they fear God and believe and do righteous deeds. And I am one of them, that is, from the first immigrants, and from the people of Badr and the people of Uhud. He said to the people: Answer the man. They remained silent. Then he said to Ibn Abbas: Answer. He said: He only sent it down as an excuse for those who He drank it from the past before it was forbidden and revealed: Indeed, wine, gambling, stones, and stones are an abomination from the work of Satan, an excuse against others. Then he asked those with him about the punishment for it, and Yahya bin Abi Talib said: If this person drinks, and if this person invents something, flog him. Eighty (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5107","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, on the authority of Abu Asim, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Rukana informed me, he said: he informed me Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not give a fatwa regarding alcohol. Ibn Abbas said: Then a man drank. He became drunk and was found leaning toward the dawn, so he took him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he approached the house of Al-Abbas, he broke free and entered upon Al-Abbas. So he adhered to it, and it was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he laughed and said: Did he do it, and he did not command me to do anything about it? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5108","Ibrahim bin Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ruh told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: I said to Ata’, Muhammad bin Ali bin told me Rukana, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He did not give anyone a fatwa regarding alcohol, so Ibn Abbas said: He drank A man got drunk and was found leaning in a forest. He was taken to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. When they approached the Abbas house, he escaped and entered on the Al-Abbas followed him behind him, so they mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he laughed and said: He did it, and then he did not give orders about it \With something\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"5109","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, on the authority of Abu al-Wadak, on the authority of Abu Sa`id Al-Khudri said: “A man was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I did not drink wine, but I drank raisins and dates mixed with water.” He said: He dabbed with the hands, beat with the sandals, and forbade dates and raisins from being mixed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5110","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Zaid Al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq Al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, He said: “A man among us was beaten forty times during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for drinking with his sandals.”"
"5111","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Abu Nu’aym, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Najrani, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: “A drunk man was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he hit him and said to him: What did you drink? He said: Wine. He said: What wine? He said: Date wine and raisins. He said: Do not mix them, each one alone is sufficient. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5112","Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Mu’alla told us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaykah, on the authority of Uqba bin Al-Harith, he said: “It was brought Al-Numan while he was drunk, caused great hardship for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he ordered those who were in the house to beat him, so they beat him. With sandals and sandals, I was among those who struck him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5113","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever drinks alcohol, flog him, then if he drinks, flog him, then if he drinks, flog him, then if he drinks, flog him.” He drank on the fourth day, and he mentioned a word meaning: So kill him. Asim bin Bahdala disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5114","Amr bin Zurarah told us, Muhammad bin Humaid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Dhakwan, on the authority of Muawiyah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever drinks alcohol, flog him, and if he returns, flog him, and if he returns, flog him, then He drank on the fourth day, so behead him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5115","Abu Bakr bin Hafs Ismail bin Hafs al-Abli told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ma`bad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Jadali, who said: I heard Muawiyah saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Who “If he drinks alcohol, flog him. Then if he returns, flog him. Then if he returns at the fourth hour, then behead him.”"
